1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,520
Today, we'll learn about Christopher Columbus, the heroic explorer who discovered America and proved the Earth was wrong.

2
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:12,220
I'm really sorry, Ms. Dazzle, but Columbus never set foot in America.

3
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:19,480
Of all the modern-day countries Columbus made it to, like Cuba, Haiti, and the Dominican Republic, none of them were in the United States.

4
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:23,940
Okay, fine. Then Columbus discovered Haiti in the Dominican Republic.

5
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:28,860
Sure he did, if you don't count the quarter million Taino people that lived there already.

6
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:33,420
The Taino treated Columbus and his crew with the utmost hospitality.

7
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:34,140
Hug?

8
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:38,220
We need the reinforcements!

9
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:47,060
Columbus repaid their kindness by returning with 17 ships and 1,200 men so he could enslave the Taino and steal their gold.

10
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:50,060
There was only one problem. They didn't have any.

11
00:00:50,460 --> 00:00:50,740
You!

12
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:51,540
Gold!

13
00:00:51,860 --> 00:00:52,120
Now!

14
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:56,320
I want to help, but what is gold?

15
00:00:56,320 --> 00:01:03,800
This infuriated Columbus, and soon, he and his crew...

16
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:04,880
I can't believe it!

17
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:07,480
I had no clue that Columbus was this cruel.

18
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:11,000
But after this, he must have gone on to do great things.

19
00:01:11,240 --> 00:01:11,760
Nope.

20
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,220
This was literally all he did.

21
00:01:14,380 --> 00:01:17,620
He didn't discover America, and he didn't prove the Earth was round.

22
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:24,420
He just bounced around the Caribbean, slaughtered a bunch of innocent people, and died thinking he had made it to India.

